{
  "_why": "Role track for TURNING, the first pack authored under docs/profiling/role-pack-authoring-guide.md. fam_machining stays the generic machining interview bound at ISCO unit 7223; this pack binds the four NCO turning occupations directly (job_domain specificity 50 beats unit 40), so a turner gets turning depth and every other machining worker is untouched.",
  "_scope": "CNC AND CONVENTIONAL, by owner ruling 2026-08-28. Binding only the two CNC codes (7223.6001/6002) made the pack reachable by exactly ONE alias phrase, 'cnc turning' — every natural Hinglish word for the trade (kharad, kharaad, खराद, lathe, लेथ, turning ka kaam) routes to 7223.0701 'Lathe Machinist' and would have fallen to the six generic machining questions. Adding 7223.0701 and 7223.0601 takes reach from one phrase to six WITHOUT touching the alias corpus. That is why the gate question says 'Turning', not 'CNC turning': a khraad operator must be able to answer it honestly. The machine question offers 'Khraad ya conventional lathe', and controller / advanced_capability both carry an escape chip, so nothing here forces a conventional turner to claim CNC skills. Pinned by packages/db/src/question-pack-reachability.test.ts.",
  "_depth": "THE TIER GATE IS turning_experience, and it is asked FIRST. It cannot be experience_years from qp_universal: phase order runs occupation_specific BEFORE universal_tail, so the universal answer does not exist yet when these items are selected. Its options carry value_number ONLY. pack-registry.service.ts resolves valueText ?? valueNumber ?? valueBool, so adding a value_text would make the answer a STRING; every gte below would then compare a string to a number, compare() returns null, and the predicate is false forever. A permanently-false ask_if is a question that is never asked, silently -- the #776 defect that sat in qp_welding for the life of the pack.",
  "_budget": "MAX_ENGINE_ASKS is 24 and qp_universal spends 8. Tier 0 is 8 items (16 total), tier 1 adds 3 (19), tier 2 adds 4 (23). One more tier-2 item would truncate the conversation of a senior worker before it closes.",
